# SYNOPSIS

```text
protocol vectraos.display.link.Link version 2
call sink() -> Sink
call edid() -> [UInt8]
event sinkChanged()
call capacity() -> UInt32
call stop()
call start(timing: Timing) throws(LinkError)
```

# DESCRIPTION

Protocol `vectraos.display.link.Link`, version 2, of library `DisplayLinkIPC`, its messages in the one wire format (wire(6)).

| Method | Kind | Since | Ordinal |
| `sink` | call | 1 | `0x1fca22af3c6f23cd` |
| `edid` | call | 1 | `0x7b19501aa665ec2a` |
| `sinkChanged` | event | 1 | `0x5a7a47f0ef1999d3` |
| `capacity` | call | 2 | `0x2328020edd05982a` |
| `stop` | call | 2 | `0x576e70afa4f14e4e` |
| `start` | call | 2 | `0x7066674ffeb8de6` |

: `edid`
  The monitor's EDID (empty without one).
: `sinkChanged`
  HPD changed, or the sink's count or EDID did: ask again.
: `capacity`
  The fastest pixel clock (kHz) the sink's best link carries at 24
  bits a pixel; 0 without a sink.
: `stop`
  The stream stopped, while the engine changes its timing.
: `start`
  The stream started for `timing`, the link trained first where the
  one up doesn't carry it.

